# CrowKV Doc Rules

Hierarchy: `requirement.md` → `design.md`/`plan.md`/`test-design.md`/`test-plan.md` → sub-topic docs (`design-xxx.md`, `plan-xxx.md`, `test-xxx-design.md`, `test-xxx-plan.md`).

Naming: lowercase-kebab-case for sub-topics.

Rules:
1. Never violate upstream. Update `requirement.md` first if a gap is found.
2. Single source of truth: requirements in `requirement.md`, design in `design.md`/`design-xxx.md`, tests in `test-design.md`/`test-xxx-design.md`.
3. Traceability: every doc references upstream docs it satisfies via section links.
4. New docs must start with:
   ```
   # CrowKV - [Type]: [Topic]
   Depends on: [upstream links]
   Satisfies: [requirement links] (design/test docs)
   ```
5. Create sub-topic docs when a topic exceeds ~200 lines or has independent phases.
6. `requirement.md` does NOT use V1/V2 annotations. Phasing belongs in `plan.md`.
